# Paid / private content
#
# The PDFs a signed-in user may download. They are deliberately NOT under
# /public — that directory is served by URL to anyone who asks, which is
# what made /sample-matt101.pdf world-readable until it was moved here.
#
# These still must not be committed. "Not served by Next" and "not in the
# repository" are different guarantees, and only the second one keeps
# them off GitHub. Two are already in history; see
# apps/web/src/lib/private-assets.ts for how they are read at runtime.
#
# Consequence of ignoring this: a Vercel build has no copies, so
# readPrivateAsset() returns null and the download routes answer
# "not found". To ship real content, put it in blob storage (Vercel Blob
# or S3) and fetch it there instead of from the filesystem.
apps/web/private-assets/

